      "function": "OT::VarSizedBinSearchArrayOf<AAT::LookupSegmentSingle<OT::IntType<unsigned short, 2u> > >::sanitize_shallow",
      "line": 835,
      "code": "return_trace (header.sanitize (c) && Type::static_size >= header.unitSize && c->check_array (bytesZ.arrayZ, header.nUnits, header.unitSize));",
      "note": "First verified project statement on the crashing path that consumes attacker-controlled `morx` bytes and creates vulnerability-relevant state. Static decoding of the staged PoC's chain subtable 5 shows a Format-2 class lookup with `unitSize = 1` and `nUnits = 4`; this vulnerable check accepts that undersized stride for `LookupSegmentSingle<HBUINT16>` elements, so the malformed lookup survives sanitization and remains reachable at the later sink.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/hb-aat-layout-morx-table.hh",
      "function": "AAT::InsertionSubtable::driver_context_t::transition",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (!before) buffer->copy_glyph ();",
      "note": "Runtime origin of the uninitialized value. The current-insert path calls `copy_glyph()` whenever `CurrentInsertBefore` is clear, but it never proves that `buffer->idx` still names an initialized input glyph before reading `info[idx]`. The saved MSAN origin chain shows that this exact call copied a never-initialized `hb_glyph_info_t` from the spare buffer capacity created by `hb_buffer_t::enlarge`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
